blocks.en:
The Z1 is controlled through the vendor’s ROS wrapper around its SDK (
              ) , with joint trajectories sent directly to the controller’s action server. In the forest campaign these were parametric sweeps between fixed joint configurations. In crop-row operation they were generated and collision-checked offline in Pinocchio Carpentier et al. (2019) , using the semantic robot description and self-collision matrix produced by the MoveIt Setup Assistant (
              ) . No motion reported in this work was planned online.

blocks.zh:
