blocks.en:
Three visualisation and simulation tools are used for different purposes. Gazebo (
              ) provides rigid-body physics for testing control and navigation. RViz (
              ) displays live or recorded sensor streams, the transform tree, costmaps and the robot model, serving both as the operator display during sessions and for diagnosing behaviour afterwards. MeshCat (
              ) provides a lightweight kinematic view without physics or controllers, which makes it the fastest way to iterate on planned motions and to confirm that sensor frame orientations match between the robot and the planner.

